  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 111 AM CDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nSunday through Friday:\n\nHigh swim risk continues into Sunday. Expect continued\nnortheasterly winds gusting 20-30 mph as low pressure slowly\nexits. No precipitation is expected, with highs in the mid to\nupper 70s. High pressure builds in Sunday night into Monday,\nbringing light and variable winds and temperatures in the low 80s\nfor Monday.\n\nLow pressure develops in the central Plains Tuesday, with a\nshortwave over Ontario showing potential for phasing with this\nlow, and bringing the next chances for precipitation to southern\nWisconsin Tuesday night through Wednesday as the resultant system\npropagates eastward (20-30%). Highs in the low to mid 80s are \nexpected both Tuesday and Wednesday.\n\nActive pattern persists through Friday, with multiple shortwaves\ndeveloping off the northern portions of the central Plains low.\nUncertainty remains in the longer term portion of the forecast as\nmodel solutions diverge, therefore kept NBM PoPs in the 15-25%\nrange Thursday and Friday.\n\nMH",
